<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Bidvest half year earnings rise 26 percent.</title>
<headline>Bidvest half year earnings rise 26 percent.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Dec 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, diluted (cts)    62.8	  vs 49.8</p>
<p>    Shr, undiluted (cts)  74.7	  vs 70.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 33.75	 vs 27.11</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   106.25	vs 78.50</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   144.76	vs 103.93</p>
<p>    Tax			 35.70	 vs 25.44</p>
<p>    Operating income	138.45	vs 107.16</p>
<p>    Turnover		  2,613.55    vs 1,963.35</p>
<p>Div payable February 28</p>
<p>on register February 21</p>
<p>Full name: Bidvest Group Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it would offer capitalisation shares in lieu of the cash dividend.</p>
<p>Manettas Ltd, in which Bidvest has a 51 percent interest, reported a major improvement in operating income for the period fro A$55,000 to A$1.825 million.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
